---
title: "daily_backup_pipeline (Daily DB Backup Workflow)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_trigger: schedule cron 0 17 * * * OR workflow_dispatch
    q_trigger --> q_install: trigger fires
    q_install --> q_dump: install postgresql-client-17
    q_dump --> q_check_dump: pg_dump DATABASE_URL --format=custom -f backup.dump
    q_check_dump --> q_encrypt: dump succeeded
    q_check_dump --> q_cleanup: dump failed
    q_encrypt --> q_check_encrypt: gpg --symmetric --cipher-algo AES256 -o backup.dump.gpg
    q_check_encrypt --> q_rm_plain: encryption succeeded
    q_check_encrypt --> q_cleanup: encryption failed
    q_rm_plain --> q_push: rm backup.dump
    q_push --> q_check_push: git clone backup-repo, cp dump, git commit, git push
    q_check_push --> q_retention: push succeeded
    q_check_push --> q_cleanup: push failed
    q_retention --> q_cleanup: delete backups older than 7 days
    q_cleanup --> [*]: rm -f backup.dump backup.dump.gpg

    note right of q_trigger
        INV-001: backup runs exactly once per day at 02:00 JST (17:00 UTC)
        INV-002: workflow_dispatch allows manual trigger at any time
    end note

    note right of q_encrypt
        INV-003: plaintext dump must be deleted after encryption (rm backup.dump)
        INV-004: GPG_PASSPHRASE must not be logged or persisted
    end note

    note right of q_cleanup
        INV-005: cleanup runs unconditionally (if: always()) regardless of prior step failures
        INV-006: no plaintext dump or encrypted file remains on runner after cleanup
    end note
